      "content": "i followed your advice and turned off basically everything—the router, the smart fridge, even the thermostat—but as soon as the house went quiet, i heard this low-frequency humming coming from inside the walls. it's not coming from the devices themselves anymore, it's like the house structure is vibrating. if the surveillance is actually embedded in the infrastructure like you're suggesting, how do people even report this? is there any way to prove this is happening to anyone else, or are we all just supposed to ignore the fact that our own homes are being turned against us?",
